From: tyn-patches <tyn-patches@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:16:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: STEINS;GATE 0 phone and RINE (SG0::Phone)

The phone of S;G0 (home screen, RINE messenger with reply choices, Amadeus,
settings, wallpapers, ringtones) is about 90 functions of Game.exe. They are
translated mechanically from a Ghidra decompile by
tools/impacto/sg0/translate_phone.py (phonecode.cpp, phoneglobals.h,
generated; do not edit) instead of being ported one by one:

- The globals of the original stay at their addresses in emulated memory
  (phoneemu.cpp), so the decompiled table accesses keep their meaning. Only
  the read only tables the phone uses (about 3 KB of numbers) are copied
  from Game.exe. ScrWork is the engine's.
- phoneshim.cpp implements the Game.exe functions the phone calls: sprites
  of the script loaded surfaces, render targets 6 / 9 as framebuffers, the
  phone's own text layout (its glyph width tables and line breaking, glyphs
  from the font sheet), hit areas registered for the next frame, flags,
  input (pad, mouse; a tap is a left click, two fingers a right click) and
  the ringtone preview on the second BGM channel.
- phonerine.cpp: instruction 10:37 (0x482df0) and the RINE conversation
  reader (0x476d50, 0x477040), which reads the script bytes itself.
- Hooks: GameSpecificType::SG0 (input before the scripts, drawing on the
  phone layers, after the message window when the original draws above it,
  and the message window's phone button), new game reset, the phone state
  (0x3ee0 bytes) in debug states.
- 01:0D MesMain sets flag 1611 while a message waits for the player, as the
  original does (0x47c620); the scripts only open the phone then.

Verified on MuMu (Android 15 x86_64 emulator, not a real device), sg0-pc
(Steam data, Chinese): the phone opens from the message window button and
closes with a right click; home, RINE, settings, wallpapers, Amadeus
"Disconnected" scene; the prologue RINE from Mayuri: reply choices cycle
with the arrows, the chosen reply is sent, the conversation runs to its end,
the phone closes and the story goes on. A debug state taken while a reply
was pending restores the conversation.

